Thanks for the steady stream of incoming bug reports.  There are
a few bugs you should know we are aware of already.  There is a shop
bug (you get segmentation if you drop items).  There are fixes needed
to get the game to compile cleanly for MSDOS, and, of course, there is
the cat problem in unpacking the game.

We cannot do anything about the cat problem since the packaging was
done by comp.sources.games (Bill Randle took time out of his vacation
to come in and distribute the game.  He did a great job, and all of us
are grateful to him.  We can live with the cat problem...).

Most of the bugs you reported thus far (and quite a few more which we
fleshed out) are already fixed, and the first official bugfixes patch
will be posted with comp.sources.games (so that it may be archived pro-
perly) at the end of this weekend.  Meanwhile, avoid dropping items in
the shop, and keep on hunting for bugs -- and please report them.

Happy hacking.

For the development team,

-Izchak


